From e428fc74af6364bd058b074f21362fb9c37d0837 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:31:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 34/38] opengl: show the views of row, column and checkerboard
 interleaved video

A picture that interleaves its views by rows, by columns or as a
checkerboard (H.264 D.2.26 types 0, 1 and 2) was shown as one picture
and never declared. Declare it as the other packings, and hand each view
over at its own resolution: the rows or the columns of the view, or its
samples of each row, each copied as it is.

The view's coordinates span the whole picture, moved by half a sample,
and its textures are sampled with GL_NEAREST, so that each pixel of the
view takes the centre of its own sample: an exact copy of 4:4:4 and RGB
pictures, and of the luma of 4:2:0 ones, whose chroma samples hold both
views. A checkerboard view is drawn one row at a time, each row moved
by half a sample to its own side. Subpictures are made for the place of
one view, as for side by side and top and bottom.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 modules/video_output/opengl/display.c     |  12 ++
 modules/video_output/opengl/vout_helper.c | 165 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/video_output/video_output.c           |   6 +
